{
  "_meta": {
    "source": "data/v1 Opp Decks/Jungle Opponent Decks v1.xlsx — Trevor's workbook, the second hand-built roster. Sheets 'J T2-1' through 'J T4'. The Index tab is the per-card classification the decks were built from, and it now carries opener archetype, trainer function, pressure and a plain-English 'wants' column.",
    "retrieved": "2026-08-21, extracted from the xlsx directly (the workbook is a zip; parsed from xl/worksheets/*.xml).",
    "scope": "The Jungle opponent roster v1, built to OPPONENTS.md's tier spec. Three T2, one T3, one T4. The two Jungle theme decks in data/jungle_decks.json stay as they are and remain the T1 intro rungs.",
    "status": "All five validate clean against Engine.prototype.validateDeck: 60 cards, no errors, no warnings, 4-copy limit respected, every card implemented.",
    "ids": "ZERO corrections were needed. Every id in the sheet's ID column resolves in CARD_DB and names the card the sheet names — checked mechanically, with accents and the NH/B2 disambiguating suffixes normalised away. Unlike data/jungle_decks.json, where three ids were wrong.",
    "nonHoloIds": "The sheet tags non-holo duplicate printings with NH (Jolteon NH = base2-20, the non-holo of base2-4). validateDeck counts copies BY NAME, so a deck holding base2-9 Pinsir and base2-25 Pinsir NH holds two Pinsir against the 4-copy limit. That is correct and it is what the sheet intends.",
    "weights": "featureWeight is Trevor's own scoring from the sheet, totalled across the deck. IT IS ONLY COMPARABLE WITHIN A ROSTER. Jungle runs 9/12/16 against Base Set's 7-7.5/10-10.5/12.5 because this set had more weight to distribute — Base Set opened evolution lines that Jungle finishes — so the five decks are scaled relative to each other, not to the previous eight. Trevor, 21 Aug 2026. See ROSTERS.md.",
    "pressure": "The pressure tags are DERIVED from the Index tab's own per-card Pressure column, tallied by copy count, rather than assigned by eye. Only three of the five earn one. Trevor's key extends OPPONENTS.md's seven with two more: HD (High Damage) and BG (Bench Growth).",
    "coverCard": "The sheet's own Cover Card field. Nothing reads it yet; PROGRESSION.md's open item 1 wants a challenger's face to be their deck's hero card, and this is that field. The Base Set workbook predates the column, so base1_decks.json has none.",
    "notInThisRoster": "Pikachu did not fit and is deferred to the next round of decks, where it will join Fossil's Raichu. Trevor, 21 Aug 2026 — the set did not separate cleanly into five decks."
  },
